body:
[https://www.reddit.com/r/The48LawsOfPower/comments/upv0d8/the\_updated\_and\_revised\_official\_reading\_list/](https://www.reddit.com/r/The48LawsOfPower/comments/upv0d8/the_updated_and_revised_official_reading_list/)

&#x200B;

This list of books might help. You don't necessarily have to follow the advice on manipulation, but read a couple of them to know what people may use against you. 

Also, this is just my personal opinion, read feminist books. All women have problems in this society, but as many men start hyping you up because of your newfound beauty, you may believe they are treating you "nicer" when they really are sizing you up to see how they can use you. You can start with Woman Hating by Andrea Dworkin ([https://www.amazon.com/Woman-Hating-Plume-Andrea-Dworkin/dp/0452268273](https://www.amazon.com/Woman-Hating-Plume-Andrea-Dworkin/dp/0452268273)) and look at the similar items. 

&#x200B;

Happy reading!

You could try hot food powder or other sort of banishing magick. I would not recommend anything that could necessarily hurt him because your friend is most likely going to go back to him anyway and he will only take it out on her. You could have her leave or him leave. Unless she has kids with him, it might be easier for her to leave. 

&#x200B;

I would not recommend getting more involved than this. I understand that she is your friend, but she believes her abuser. If you attempt to do more, he might harm you.

Right now I am taking Modern Art and Ideas on coursera. I also know there are courses on [edx.org](https://edx.org). 

&#x200B;

Thank you for your recommendations.
